{
  "description": {
    "what_this_is": "One row per run, merged from the per-run metrics.json files in experiments/runs/. Values are copied verbatim from those files; nothing is recomputed here.",
    "reading_notes": [
      "`ari`, `nmi`, `rare_f1`, `n_clusters`, `ari_vs_pseudo` come from the `scformer` block: the model's own output.",
      "`ari_initial_partition` and `rare_f1_initial_partition` describe the partition a run started from, before training. This is the reference a dynamic-clustering run must beat to show it preserved its own starting structure. The `initial_partition_source` field on each row says where the value came from, because it is not the same source in every run: either the warm-up cluster partition (`dynamic.initial_partition`) or the A0 pseudo-label (recorded under `leiden_baseline` for runs whose `init_source` is `a0_pseudo`). Rows with neither are stage 0/1 runs, which have no such start.",
      "`ari_leiden_reference` and `rare_f1_leiden_reference` come from the `leiden_baseline` block: the upstream Leiden partition. It answers a different question (did the model beat the free baseline) and must not be read as a run's starting partition; on the same run the two differ, 0.3298 vs 0.0813.",
      "`ari_vs_pseudo` is agreement with the training pseudo-label, not with truth. A value near 1.0 means the model reproduced its target; see the report's headroom discussion. It is absent for stage 0, which has no such target.",
      "`spatial_relation` is whether the spot-to-spot spatial relation was enabled. The source files record this under two different key names depending on stage; they are merged here.",
      "`pseudo_resolution` is the Leiden resolution that produced the training target. 0.5 yields no cluster below the 4.5% rarity threshold, so rare_f1 is pinned at 0 there; 0.8 does yield one, so rare_f1 is non-zero before any model runs.",
      "Runs whose name contains `preflight`, `probe` or `warmuponly` are historical exploration, not the formal arms. `T30` runs use a 30-epoch refresh interval where the default is 10."
    ],
    "evidence_index": {
      "frozen_target_headroom": {
